Round 17 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
- Removed compiled-path APP-frame materialization by introducing a local raw-arg ABI:
  - `HvmAotFn` now takes `(stack, s_pos, base, a_args, a_pos)`.
  - `aot_call_ref(...)` forwards local args through compiled->compiled calls.
  - `aot_try_call(...)` now allocates a local `a_args[AOT_ARG_CAP]` and reifies pending args back to runtime APP frames only at the interpreter boundary.
  - Added helpers:
    - `aot_stack_push_arg(...)`
    - `aot_stack_reify_args(...)`
- Emitter (`emit.c`) now lowers head-position args to local arg stack:
  - head `APP`: pushes arg into `a_args` instead of `aot_alloc(...APP_FRAME_HEAD)`.
  - head `LAM`: consumes from `a_args` first, then falls back to runtime stack APP frames.
  - head `SWI`: peeks/forces from `a_args` first; writes back forced arg into `a_args` slot.
  - head `MAT`: peeks/forces from `a_args` first; on matched branch pushes ctor fields into `a_args` (no APP-frame heap alloc).
  - head `REF`: calls `aot_call_ref(id, stack, s_pos, base, a_args, a_pos)`.
  - Generated function signature updated accordingly.
- Reduced env bind-list allocation pressure:
  - `aot_env_get(...)` no longer calls `aot_env_head(...)` for prefix materialization.
  - It now lazily allocates only the requested slot when missing.
  - `aot_env_head(...)` remains for deopt/fallback list construction/rewiring.

Why
- Round 16 telemetry showed massive allocation in `APP_FRAME_*` and `ENV_BIND` despite near-zero deopts.
- The compiled evaluator was still emulating runtime APP/env structures eagerly.
- This round moves compiled execution toward register/local-array argument passing, with heap representation only at boundary crossings.

