Key insight (updated)
- APP/env materialization was indeed a dominant bottleneck on many kernels; removing it yields substantial speedups and large allocation drops.
- After this change, explicit compiled-site allocation is often dominated by `DUP_CELL`.
- `edit_dist` still shows huge total heap vs tiny `AOT_ALLOC`, confirming substantial allocation outside currently attributed AOT sites (likely generic runtime interactions/forcing paths).

